# Navigation Tab Enhancement Implementation Tasks

## Overview
Enhance navigation tabs with contextual information and move language settings to be per-provider instead of global.

## Task 1: Enhance TabButton Component in SettingsTabView.swift
- Add subtitle parameter to TabButton struct
- Add status indicator support (optional green checkmark)
- Update TabButton view to display subtitle below title
- Keep minimalist design with smaller, muted subtitle text

## Task 2: Provider Tab Enhancement
- Modify ProviderSettingsView to check API key validity on appear
- Pass current provider info to TabButton:
  - Title: "Provider"
  - Subtitle: "OpenAI • EN" (or "Groq • Auto", etc.)
  - Status: Show green checkmark if API key is valid
- Update SettingsTabView to compute and pass this information

## Task 3: Audio Tab Enhancement  
- Pass selected microphone name to TabButton:
  - Title: "Audio"
  - Subtitle: Show microphone name or "No mic selected"
- Update SettingsTabView to get microphone name from SettingsManager

## Task 4: Move Language Setting to Per-Provider Storage
- Update SettingsManager:
  - Remove global `transcriptionLanguage` property
  - Add per-provider language properties:
    - `openAILanguage: String = "auto"`
    - `groqLanguage: String = "auto"` 
    - `deepgramLanguage: String = "auto"`
  - Add method `getCurrentLanguage() -> String` that returns language for current provider
  - Update Keys enum and save/load methods

## Task 5: Update Provider Settings UI
- In ProviderSettingsView:
  - Remove global languageConfigurationSection
  - Add language picker inside modelConfigurationSection
  - Order: Language picker → Model picker
  - Use compact/inline style for minimalist look
  - Only show language picker for current provider

## Task 6: Update RecordingSettingsView
- Remove languageConfigurationSection entirely
- Language is now configured per-provider, not globally

## Task 7: Update API Calls
- Update TranscriptionService and AI provider implementations
- Use SettingsManager.getCurrentLanguage() instead of transcriptionLanguage
- Ensure each provider passes its specific language setting

## Implementation Notes
- Keep all UI changes minimalist and hacker-friendly
- Avoid excessive visual elements
- Use system fonts and standard spacing
- Subtitle text should be smaller and secondary color
- API key validation should be fast and non-blocking
- Cache validation results to avoid repeated API calls

